{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 57, :comments ["<b>And they turned back</b> — a nif'al form, from the root ס-ג, like ויכונו." "<b>Like their fathers</b> — in the days of the Judges." "<b>They turned like a deceitful bow.</b> Rabbi Moses said: רמיה is an adjective modifying קשת, and the meaning is like 'an idle/crooked male' [זכר עצל], a noun, like 'and it shall be for a deceit [ורמיה תהיה למס].' In my opinion: רמיה is a noun, like 'the foundation [והשתיה] as decreed [כדת],' like 'the drawing of a bow [רומי קשת].' The proof: 'deceitful [רמיה]' followed by 'the arrows of a mighty man, sharp [ואחריו חצי גבור שנונים].' The meaning is: the bow turns and does not deceive the one who draws it [הרומה], or its meaning is as I explained regarding the word 'they turned [הפכו] on the day of battle'; therefore he now explains what he mentioned earlier."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:20.962648171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}